  "name": "Yola",
  "description": "Yola is the capital of Adamawa State in northeastern Nigeria and the seat of the historic Adamawa Emirate. It lies along the Benue River and serves as a major commercial and cultural hub in the region. Known for its Fulani heritage, traditional markets (e.g., Jimeta Modern Market), colonial-era buildings, the American University of Nigeria (AUN), and scenic river views, Yola blends Islamic culture, diverse ethnic influences, and natural beauty. Nearby attractions include the Gashaka-Gumti National Park (one of Africa's largest), the Upper Benue River, and historical sites tied to the 19th-century jihad and emirate history.",
